course: dictionary
lesson: 1371
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can often tell which meaning the writer means by reading the words around it. The word canvas is a good example, and its context gives you the clues.
explain: «Very thick paint that sticks out from the canvas is called impasto.» Here a canvas is the cloth stretched on a frame that a painter works on. In «The Colosseum in Rome had a canvas roof for shade», canvas is the strong, heavy cloth itself. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence?
explain: On a computer, canvas means something else again. In an app like Scratch, the canvas is the area on the screen where you draw or design. Try each meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Canvas is a strong, heavy cloth used for tents, sails, bags and shoes.
fact: A canvas can be a piece of this cloth stretched on a frame for painting, or the painting itself.
fact: In computing, the canvas is the area on the screen where you draw or design.
fact: «Under canvas» means living in a tent, camping.
fact: Canvas is a different word from canvass, so do not mix them up.
exercise: «Very thick paint that sticks out from the canvas is called impasto.» In this sentence, what is a canvas? | *A piece of cloth stretched on a frame for a painting | The area on a screen where you draw | A strong cloth used for making tents | A pair of trousers
exercise: Mum says, «We are going to sleep under canvas this weekend.» What does this mean? | We will sleep in a tall castle | *We will sleep in a tent, camping | We will paint the bedroom walls | We will sleep on the beach in the sun
exercise: In a computing lesson, the teacher says, «Draw a star on the canvas.» Where should you draw the star? | In a paint tin | On your canvas shoes | In a notebook on your desk | *On the area of the screen where the app lets you draw
test: Alfie looks at «a canvas of one colour» in the Tate Modern. What is a canvas here? | The screen of a computer | A tent for camping | A strong bag | *A painting, or the cloth it is painted on
test: In Kipling's story, the man wears blue canvas «breeches». What are breeches? | Shoes | *Trousers | Braces that hold trousers up | A folding pocket-knife
exam: The Colosseum had a «canvas roof for shade». Which meaning of canvas fits here? | The screen of a computer | A painting hung on a wall | *A strong, heavy cloth | A kind of food
